    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A measured movement with an unmeasured cadenza inside it (docs/plan/prompts/74)." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The cadenza is `senza { ... }`: the barlines stop for exactly as long as the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// braces say and the meter that resumes is the one that was already in force," },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// so there is no second meter statement to keep in step with the first." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// What it costs is the thing worth pointing at. An unmeasured stretch is one" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// measure — measure 5 here — and the measure number does not advance across" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// it, so the movement resumes at measure 6. That is not a limitation of the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// representation; it is how a conductor's score numbers a cadenza, and the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// alternative design (barlines with gaps in them) would have numbered it" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// wrong while looking more faithful." },
